---
// YouTubeEmbed.astro — V-1 Phase A. The single authority for CLICK-TO-PLAY YouTube video.
//
// PHASE A SHIPS THIS WITH NO CALLERS. Nothing imports it yet, so it renders nowhere and
// changes no byte of `dist/`. That is the same ordering AR-2 B-2 used for the bidi
// formatter: introduce the authority in one commit, migrate callers in another, so no
// single commit both defines a contract and moves the corpus.
//
// THE INVARIANT (gate 4l, specified in docs/perf/V1-video-facade.md §6.1.1):
// no page, layout, `page-content` block or MDX body writes `youtube.com/embed` directly.
// A caller names a video and receives an embed.
//
// WHY THIS COMPONENT NO LONGER HAS AN `ambient` MODE.
// The brief's §2 gave one component two modes. Splitting them is the owner's call, taken
// while there are still zero callers — the only moment it is free, since afterwards it is
// 40 call sites across 8 locale blocks.
//
// The two modes were never two presentations of one thing. They differ in provider
// commitment, which is the axis that matters:
//
//   facade    256 on-demand carousel slides. YouTube is CANONICAL and permanent here —
//             these are full uploads with their own watch pages, and nothing in V-1 or
//             after it proposes moving them. This component.
//   ambient   40 decorative muted loops. YouTube is one possible BACKEND, and the
//             repository evidence (V1-video-facade.md §7.2) leans toward self-hosting a
//             trimmed loop instead. AmbientVideo.astro.
//
// Naming the backend in this component's identity is therefore correct: for `facade` the
// backend is the contract. Abstracting all 296 placements behind a provider-neutral
// interface would generalize 256 that have no swap story in order to protect 40 that do,
// and would blunt gate 4l from a fixed-string grep into a parser.
//
// WHY THERE IS NO <script> HERE. This project ships zero JS bundles — every script in the
// corpus is `is:inline`, and `dist/` contains no `_astro/` directory. An `is:inline` script
// inside this component would be duplicated once per instance, which on `/utv/` means 21
// copies of the same listener. Activation is therefore ONE delegated listener in
// `BaseLayout.astro`, matching the analytics instrumentation already there, and it lands in
// Phase B with the first facade caller — adding it in Phase A would change all 620 pages,
// which is exactly what Phase A promises not to do.
//
// This component emits markup and state. It runs nothing.
import { t } from '../../lib/ui';

interface Props {
  /** The 11-character YouTube id. The only identity gate 4m records. */
  videoId: string;
  /** Human title. Required: it is the accessible name of the play control. */
  title: string;
  lang?: string;
  class?: string;
}

const { videoId, title, lang = 'en', class: className } = Astro.props;

if (!/^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{11}$/.test(videoId)) {
  // Fail at build time rather than rendering a broken embed. A malformed id produces a
  // player that 404s silently in an iframe, which no gate and no visitor reports.
  throw new Error(`YouTubeEmbed: "${videoId}" is not a YouTube video id (11 chars of [A-Za-z0-9_-])`);
}

// `hqdefault`, never `maxresdefault`. maxres does not exist for every upload and YouTube
// answers a missing one with a 120x90 grey placeholder rather than a 404 — an invisible
// failure that cannot be feature-detected.
//
// Measured 2026-07-28, closing the ⚠ in V1-video-facade.md §1.3a: all six videos that
// currently carry a poster DO have a real maxres (109–306 KB, not the ~2 KB placeholder),
// so the homepage's existing `maxresdefault` hero is not degraded today. The rule stands
// anyway — it is about the uploads nobody has checked yet, and about the fact that the
// failure mode is silent. A rule that only holds for the corpus it was measured on is a
// coincidence.
const thumb = `https://i.ytimg.com/vi/${videoId}/hqdefault.jpg`;
---

<div class:list={['yt-embed', 'yt-embed--facade', className]} style="aspect-ratio:16/9;position:relative;">
  <button
    type="button"
    class="yt-embed__activate"
    data-yt-facade={videoId}
    aria-label={t('a11y.playVideo', lang, { title })}
    style="all:unset;display:block;width:100%;height:100%;cursor:pointer;position:relative;"
  >
    {/* alt="" is deliberate: the button carries the accessible name, so a described
        thumbnail would make a screen reader announce the same video twice. */}
    <img src={thumb} alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="480" height="360"
         style="width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;display:block;" />
  </button>
</div>
